      "bio_summary": {
        "value": "Born and raised in a Philadelphia rowhome, Brendan Boyle worked hard to achieve the American Dream. Brendan learned the value of hard work from his father, a SEPTA maintenance custodian who emigrated from Ireland at the age of 19, and his mother, a school crossing guard. Brendan was the first in his family to attend college and received a scholarship to attend the University of Notre Dame. Brendan would later earn his Master’s Degree in public policy from Harvard University’s John F. Kennedy School of Government.",
